MERGE (n:Section {id: "sec_stat_004_3"}) ON CREATE SET number: "3", heading: "Communication, acceptance and revocation of proposals. The communication of", act_title: "Contract Act, 1872", act_id: "act_stat_004", text_preview: "3. Communication, acceptance and revocation of proposals. The communication of proposals, the acceptance of proposals, and the revocation of proposals and acceptances, res- pectively, are deemed to be";
MERGE (n:Section {id: "sec_stat_004_4"}) ON CREATE SET number: "4", heading: "Communication when complete. The communication of a proposal is complete when it", act_title: "Contract Act, 1872", act_id: "act_stat_004", text_preview: "4. Communication when complete. The communication of a proposal is complete when it comes to the knowledge of the person to whom it is made. The communication of an acceptance is complete,___ has agai";
MERGE (n:Section {id: "sec_stat_004_5"}) ON CREATE SET number: "5", heading: "Revocation of proposals and acceptances. A proposal may be revoked at any time before", act_title: "Contract Act, 1872", act_id: "act_stat_004", text_preview: "5. Revocation of proposals and acceptances. A proposal may be revoked at any time before the communication of its acceptance is complete as against the proposer, but not afterwards. An acceptance may ";
MERGE (n:Section {id: "sec_stat_004_6"}) ON CREATE SET number: "6", heading: "Revocation how made. A proposal is revoked—", act_title: "Contract Act, 1872", act_id: "act_stat_004", text_preview: "6. Revocation how made. A proposal is revoked— (1) by the communication of notice of revocation by the proposer to the other party ; (2) by the lapse of the time prescribed in such proposal for its ac";
MERGE (n:Section {id: "sec_stat_004_7"}) ON CREATE SET number: "7", heading: "Acceptance must be absolute. In order to convert a proposal into a promise, the", act_title: "Contract Act, 1872", act_id: "act_stat_004", text_preview: "7. Acceptance must be absolute. In order to convert a proposal into a promise, the acceptance must__ (1) be absolute and unqualified ; (2) be expressed in some usual and reasonable manner, unless the ";
